%description:

RFC 9000 -- connection establishment.

Checks RFC9000-PKT-1, RFC9000-PKT-2 (description), RFC9000-SIZE-1 (must), from
doc/project/evidence/standard/rfc9000/catalog.md. The English procedure and mockup are in
doc/project/evidence/protocol/quic/checks/establishment.md#connection-establishment; the program steps below map
one to one onto its expected observations (steps 1+2 share one datagram, since observations 1 and 2
both describe that same first datagram). Mockup mapping: host A = client, host B = server.

Scenario: client opens a QUIC connection to server and sends 4000 octets on one stream (the
checks.md common-mockup constant), via TrafficgenCompound+QuicTrafficgen+TrafficgenSimple (a
single 4000B burst; QuicClient, the app used in examples/quic/basic3, cannot be reused here
because it hardcodes two fixed writes of 1000B and 500B in C++ (QuicClient.cc,
socketEstablished()), not a configurable size). packetInterval is set far beyond
sim-time-limit and packetCount left at -1 (infinite) so the generator's own "all done, tell
the handler to close" path (QuicTrafficgen::handleGeneratorInfo, TRAFFICGEN_INFO_FINISH) never
fires -- otherwise the client would call quic socket close() immediately after handing the
4000B to the socket, which (per RFC9000-CLOSE-1 / Rfc9000ConnectionClose.test) sends
CONNECTION_CLOSE right away and would race the handshake/short-header observations below.

Implementation note (Task 0 probe finding): QUIC has no protocol dissector registered
(src/inet/transportlayer/quic has no Register_Protocol_Dissector for Protocol::quic), so
PacketDissector falls back to DefaultProtocolDissector, which visits the whole undissected
remainder as one opaque chunk -- confirmed empirically: evalPacketField(pkt,
"InitialPacketHeader.version") and friends all threw "protocol '...' not present in packet",
at every observation point tried (client.udp, both directions, all four recognized
signals). This test therefore never uses .packet("quic....") or evalPacketField() for QUIC
fields; it walks the packet's own chunk tree directly via QuicChunks.h's
findQuicChunk<T>(), which *does* work reliably (also confirmed empirically) because
inet::quic::QuicPacket::createOmnetPacket() builds each QUIC packet by insertAtBack()-ing
distinct FieldsChunk-derived chunks, which INET represents as a flat SequenceChunk --
including the UDP header, still flattened in rather than nested, at an observation point
before UDP pops it. .packet("udp....") for plain UDP fields is unaffected (UDP has its own
registered dissector) and works normally, though this test does not need it.

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "QuicChunks.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("rfc9000_connection_establishment")
        // Expected observations 1 and 2: the first UDP datagram from host A to host B
        // carries a QUIC packet with a long header naming QUIC version 1 (RFC9000-PKT-1;
        // confirms the stimulus -- a connection attempt started), and that same datagram
        // is at least 1200 octets (RFC9000-SIZE-1) -- the honest reading of "the UDP
        // datagram that carries the Initial packet" is the whole datagram UDP hands to
        // IP, byteLength here, which already includes the 8-octet UDP header.
        .once(on("client.udp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .match([](const MatchContext& c) {
                      auto initial = findQuicChunk<InitialPacketHeader>(c.event.packet);
                      return initial != nullptr
                          && initial->getVersion() == 1
                          && c.event.packet->getByteLength() >= 1200;
                  })
                  .describe("host A's first datagram: a long-header Initial packet, version 1, >= 1200 octets")
                  .within(0.5))
        // Expected observation 3: host B answers with a datagram carrying a long header
        // packet -- the handshake proceeds in both directions.
        .once(on("server.udp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .match([](const MatchContext& c) {
                      return findQuicChunk<LongPacketHeader>(c.event.packet) != nullptr;
                  })
                  .describe("host B's answering datagram, also a long-header packet")
                  .within(0.5))
        // Expected observation 4: later, host A sends a datagram carrying a QUIC packet
        // with a short header (RFC9000-PKT-2) -- the connection reached the state in
        // which application data travels.
        .once(on("client.udp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .match([](const MatchContext& c) {
                      return findQuicChunk<ShortPacketHeader>(c.event.packet) != nullptr;
                  })
                  .describe("host A's later datagram: a short-header (1-RTT) packet")
                  .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
// present only so opp_test compiles the %global above; this module is not in the network.
EV << "rfc9000_connection_establishment compiled\n";

%file: test.ned

import inet.node.inet.StandardHost;
import inet.node.ethernet.Eth100M;
import inet.networklayer.configurator.ipv4.Ipv4NetworkConfigurator;

// Mockup of doc/project/evidence/protocol/quic/checks.md's "Common mockup":
// host A (client) -- path P -- host B (server).
network QuicNet
{
    submodules:
        configurator: Ipv4NetworkConfigurator { @display("p=100,50"); }
        client: StandardHost { @display("p=250,100"); }
        server: StandardHost { @display("p=450,100"); }
    connections:
        client.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> server.ethg++;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
network = QuicNet
sim-time-limit = 5s
seed-set = 0

**.quic.typename = "Quic"

# client: a single 4000-octet burst on one stream (checks.md's common-mockup data block).
**.client.hasQuic = true
**.client.numApps = 1
**.client.app[0].typename = "TrafficgenCompound"
**.client.app[0].numGenerators = 1
**.client.app[0].generator[0].typename = "TrafficgenSimple"
**.client.app[0].generator[0].id = 0
**.client.app[0].generator[0].packetSize = 4000B
**.client.app[0].generator[0].packetCount = -1
**.client.app[0].generator[0].packetInterval = 10s
**.client.app[0].generator[0].startTime = 0.1s
**.client.app[0].generator[0].ordered = false
**.client.app[0].handler.typename = "QuicTrafficgen"
**.client.app[0].handler.localPort = 1001
**.client.app[0].handler.connectPort = 1000
**.client.app[0].handler.connectAddress = "server"

# server: reads and discards everything it receives.
**.server.hasQuic = true
**.server.numApps = 1
**.server.app[*].typename = "QuicDiscardServer"
**.server.app[*].localAddress = ""
**.server.app[*].localPort = 1000

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST rfc9000_connection_establishment: PASS
